coi ro do

I and a couple of other lojbanists have been working=20
to improve the look, feel and content of the front-end=20
pages of the Lojban wiki.  We have encountered a=20
technical problem and would really appreciate some=20
help.

The problem in question is the translation of certain=20
words in the wiki interface (particularly the left-side=20
menu).  Most words can easily be translated using=20
the Edit languages tables - and this has already been=20
done with Spanish and Hungarian.  However this=20
easy non-technical method doesn't work for certain=20
accented letters.  For example, Spanish Comit=E9 ends=20
up as Comit&eacute.  Doesn't look good!


I've asked the Tiki forum for advice, and they=20
have referred me to:
http://doc.tikiwiki.org/Translating+interface

Well, so far the translations have been done by=20
non-technical newbies (like me). Our technical=20
skills are not up to this new challenge.  And that=20
is very discouraging for future translations!

Is there anybody reading this that would like to help?
We can provide you with the translated words,=20
probably no more than 20 in all.  It doesn't look like=20
a lot of work - for anybody who has done any coding.
Also, Rick may need to provide you with access to=20
the language files.

totus

